# MS Kanzlei – Project Structure

Reference for where source files and key config live. Paths are from project root.

## Root

| File / folder | Purpose |
|---------------|--------|
| `content/` | MDX page content (home, legal areas, impressum) |
| `src/` | Application source (app, components, lib) |
| `public/` | Static assets (images, icons) |
| `e2e/` | Playwright end-to-end tests |
| `docs/` | Project documentation |
| `next.config.ts` | Next.js config (static export, image optimization) |
| `package.json` | Scripts and dependencies |
| `tsconfig.json` | TypeScript config |
| `components.json` | shadcn/ui config |
| `playwright.config.ts` | Playwright e2e config |
| `export-images.config.js` | next-export-optimize-images config |
| `eslint.config.mjs` | ESLint config |
| `postcss.config.mjs` | PostCSS config |
| `CLAUDE.md` | Project overview for AI (commands, architecture, key files) |

## `content/`

MDX pages; slug comes from filename (without `.mdx`).

- `home.mdx` – homepage (route `/`)
- `arbeitsrecht.mdx`, `datenschutz.mdx`, `gesellschaftsrecht.mdx`, `insolvenzrecht.mdx`, `mietrecht.mdx` – legal area pages
- `impressum.mdx` – legal imprint

## `src/`

### `src/app/`

Next.js App Router.

- `layout.tsx` – root layout (Nav, Footer, theme)
- `page.tsx` – homepage (renders `content/home.mdx`)
- `[slug]/page.tsx` – dynamic route for other MDX pages; `generateStaticParams()` from content slugs
- `favicon.ico` – favicon

### `src/components/`

React components.

- `header.tsx`, `footer.tsx`, `hero.tsx` – layout and landing
- `mdx-components.tsx` – custom MDX components for next-mdx-remote
- `dark-veil.tsx`, `testimonial.tsx`, `theme-provider.tsx` – UI/theme
- `ui/` – shadcn-style primitives: `button`, `card`, `container`, `dropdown-menu`, `icons`, `logo`, `mode-toggle`, `separator`, `typography`

### `src/lib/`

Shared logic, config, styles.

- `mdx.ts` – read/parse MDX from `content/`, frontmatter, slugs
- `config.json` – app/site config
- `types.ts` – shared TypeScript types
- `utils/cn.ts` – class-name merge utility
- `hooks/use-mobile.ts` – mobile breakpoint hook
- `styles/` – Tailwind and themes:
  - `globals.css` – global styles; theme import (e.g. gingerhero)
  - `theme.css` – theme wiring
  - `variables-*.css` – per-theme CSS variables (amethysthaze, bubblegum, caffeine, candyland, gingerhero, nature, sageandsand, vintagepaper)
  - `fonts/` – font theme modules (`index.ts`, `index.node.ts`, and one file per theme)

## `public/`

Static assets; reference with paths like `/images/...`.

- `images/icons/` – SVG icons (e.g. icon-blog-teaser.svg, icon-code.svg)
- `images/rechtsanwalt-mark-schilling.jpg` – lawyer photo

## `e2e/`

- `home.spec.ts` – Playwright e2e for homepage

## `.cursor/`

- `rules/` – Cursor rule files (`.mdc`)
- `commands/` – Cursor command definitions

## Path aliases

- `@/*` → `./src/*`
- `@/components/*` → `./src/components/*`
- `@/lib/*` → `./src/lib/*`
- `@/img/*` → `./public/img/*` (if used)

When adding features: put pages in `content/`, routes in `src/app/`, shared UI in `src/components/`, and content/config/theme logic in `src/lib/`.
